# lens.env — forwarded WHOLESALE into the lens container (docker-compose.yaml `env_file:`).
# Copy to `lens.env`. Every variable is optional; unset keeps the documented default, and the file
# itself is optional (`required: false`), so a deployment without it boots unchanged.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS NOT `.env`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT.
#   .env      = the compose PROJECT file. It feeds ${VAR} substitution for every service, and on the
#               deployed box the procedure in talyvor-suite (deploy/README.md:470-476) appends
#               TRACK_GATEWAY_AUTH_SECRET and DOCS_GATEWAY_AUTH_SECRET to it, because
#               track-docs.compose.yaml runs in this project. Lens has no use for those and must not
#               receive them.
#   lens.env  = LENS_* only, delivered to the lens container and nowhere else.
#
# ⚠⚠ DO NOT PUT A VARIABLE HERE IF docker-compose.yaml ALSO LISTS IT IN `environment:`.
# Compose's `environment:` OVERRIDES `env_file`, and the curated entries are written
# `- LENS_X=${LENS_X:-}`, which resolves from .env / the shell. If .env does not define it that
# resolves to EMPTY — and the empty WINS over whatever you put here. Verified in a real container:
# a variable set in lens.env and also listed in environment: arrives as "".
#
# So the two files are not interchangeable, and the split is by MECHANISM, not by importance:
#   .env      → the curated critical set (the variables docker-compose.yaml names explicitly, kept
#               visible in the deployment file). Set them THERE.
#   lens.env  → everything else — the long tail compose does not name.
# internal/config/lens_env_shadow_test.go fails the build if the two ever overlap, because the
# overlap is silent: a correct-looking value that is discarded.
#
# ⚠ MIGRATING FROM #375: that revision briefly forwarded `.env` itself. If you put LENS_* variables
# there expecting them to reach the process, MOVE THEM HERE. The curated `environment:` list in
# docker-compose.yaml still covers the critical set either way, so nothing critical breaks meanwhile.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ MONEY-PATH CONTROLS. A control you cannot reach is a SAFETY VALVE WELDED SHUT — the default
# may be fine; what you have lost is the ability to CHANGE it. The mint caps are the sharpest
# case: a cap exists for the moment something is minting too fast, which is exactly the moment
# it would be unreachable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_SETTLEMENT_FAIL_CLOSED_ENABLED=true   # default FALSE — the protection you turn ON
# LENS_LXC_RESERVATION_ENABLED=false         # default TRUE — the documented ROLLBACK path
# LENS_LXC_AGENT_ALLOCATION_ENABLED=false    # the immediate-debit fallback
# LENS_LXC_RESERVATION_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=4096
# LENS_GATEWAY_PRICE_CEILING=                # price ceiling; must be > 0 when set
# LENS_POOL_MINT_CAP_PER_ENTRY=
# LENS_POOL_MINT_CAP_PER_PAIR=
# LENS_POOL_MINT_CAP_WINDOW=
# LENS_DISTILL_MINT_CAP_PER_CONTENT=
# LENS_DISTILL_MINT_CAP_PER_PAIR=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ CROSS-TENANT POOLING SAFETY. The margin is a property of the CONFIGURED EMBEDDER, not a
# constant. The default below is the measured, shipped configuration; a weaker model narrows the
# margin, and what the margin protects is one workspace's answer being served to another.
# Changing this for embedding cost is exactly the trade that looks free and is not.
# Lens WARNS at boot if this is changed while pooling is on. Verify with `lens poolcheck`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# LENS_SEMANTIC_THRESHOLD is declared in docker-compose.yaml (default 0.98) and set in .env, not here (B9.4):
# the compose entry would override a value set in this file.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STORED ANSWERS ARE KEPT UNTIL SOMEONE DELETES THEM (B21.2). Unset (the default) = an answer is
# served regardless of its age and the hourly sweeper never deletes it, private and shared alike;
# only quality eviction and deletion by the workspace remove one. A self-hosted operator may set a
# Go duration (h/m/s, e.g. 504h = 21 days): an answer unused for that long is then no longer served
# and is deleted, and each reuse restarts its clock.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_SEMANTIC_CACHE_RETENTION=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPERATOR ALERTING
# ⚠ Leave the operator webhook UNSET until a receiver exists. Nothing accepts its `catalog_drift`
# payload today; Track's /v1/lens/webhook returns 200 for unknown types, which this client reads
# as DELIVERED and never retries.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BATCH LANE — OFF, and setting this alone will NOT open it
# /v1/batch/* submits straight to Anthropic without entering serve(): Talyvor pays the provider
# and the workspace is charged nothing, because BatchRouter.SetSettleHook has no production
# caller. The lane also takes its workspace from a client header without authorizing it, and
# /v1/batch/jobs returns every workspace's jobs — prompts and responses included.
# The gate is a CONJUNCTION (see cmd/lens/batch_routes.go): the routes register only when this is
# true AND a settle hook is wired. Setting it today logs an ERROR and leaves the lane closed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_BATCH_ENABLED=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SYNTHETIC USERS (B17.1) — OFF unless this is set
# The operator key for POST /v1/synthetic/workspaces {"count":100} (creates synthetic test
# workspaces, each with test credits and a token) and POST /v1/synthetic/workspaces/reset (clears
# their stored answers and restores their credits). Send it as X-Talyvor-Synthetic-Key. Unset, the
# routes are not registered and answer 404. A synthetic workspace's money is test money: it moves only
# among synthetic workspaces, and its pooled answers are shared only with other synthetic workspaces.
# B25.7: the same key brings a synthetic workspace's slow money due now, so one tester run sees it —
# POST /v1/synthetic/workspaces/{ws}/loans/{loan}/due, …/marketplace/bill/pay,
# …/marketplace/bill/{invoice}/refund and …/agents/{agent}/card/authorizations, and B32.102's …/card-link
# links two of them as though they paid with one card; a real workspace gets 403.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_SYNTHETIC_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEST USERS PAY IN STRIPE TEST MODE (B25.2) — a synthetic workspace cannot buy or subscribe until set
# A synthetic workspace always tops up and subscribes through Stripe TEST MODE (test card 4242 4242 4242
# 4242), even once LENS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is live; its credits, allowance and royalties are marked test,
# never paid out and never counted in real totals. Needs LENS_BILLING_ENABLED. The key must be a test-mode
# key (a live key stops Lens starting). In Stripe (test mode): Developers → Webhooks → add the endpoint
# https://<lens host>/v1/billing/webhook/test with the same events as the billing webhook; its signing
# secret goes here. The plans are the test-mode Price ids, in LENS_BILLING_SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS's form
# (plus=price_…,pro=price_…,max=price_…); unset, they are the active Prices the test-mode account holds under
# the lookup keys talyvor_plus_monthly, talyvor_pro_monthly and talyvor_max_monthly (B17.21), and BYOK's,
# Team's and Business's — talyvor_byok_monthly ($199), talyvor_team_monthly ($49) and talyvor_business_monthly
# ($299), which Lens creates in a test-mode account that lacks them (B27.26, B32.10); in live mode Nicolai creates
# them in Stripe under the same lookup keys, and code never does. Enterprise is not a Stripe Price: the operator
# records the contract (PUT /v1/admin/workspaces/{id}/contract). While
# LENS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is itself a test-mode key and the key and secret below are unset, a synthetic
# workspace tops up and subscribes through it, and LENS_BILLING_SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS unset is looked up the same way.
# B25.6 — its marketplace bill, seller payouts (Connect) and agent cards (Issuing) go through the same
# test-mode key and webhook: make the marketplace meter and metered Price again in test mode (as under THE
# MARKETPLACE BILL below) and put that Price id here; unset, a synthetic workspace cannot use a paid
# listing (while LENS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is itself a test key it may be the same Price as
# LENS_MARKET_BILL_PRICE_ID). Add the Issuing events (issuing_authorization.updated,
# issuing_transaction.created) to the test-mode endpoint too. LENS_STRIPE_ISSUING_WEBHOOK_SECRET stays the
# TEST-MODE real-time endpoint's secret.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_SUBSCRIPTION_PLANS=
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_MARKET_BILL_PRICE_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AGENT APPROVALS WITH A PASSKEY, AND A PUSH WHEN ONE IS FILED (B19.16)
# Passkeys are created for LENS_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID from the pages in LENS_WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS (comma-
# separated). Once a workspace's owner registers one, approving or denying an agent's request takes
# a passkey assertion. LENS_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY signs the web push sent to the owner's devices when an
# approval is filed — generate one with `lens vapid-key`; unset, no push is sent and the push routes
# answer 404. LENS_VAPID_SUBJECT is the contact the browsers' push services are given.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=app.talyvor.com
# LENS_WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS=https://app.talyvor.com
# LENS_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# LENS_VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:support@talyvor.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE PHONE APP'S DEVICE KEYS (B40.4) — a phone's hardware key signs approvals and mandates as a
# passkey does. LENS_DEVICE_APPLE_APP_ID is the iPhone app's "<team id>.<bundle id>" its App Attest
# attestations must be for; empty, no iPhone key registers (Android keys check against Google's roots).
# LENS_DEVICE_TEST_ATTESTATION=true accepts keys with a fake attestation (platform "test"): for test
# stacks only, never on a server real people use.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_DEVICE_APPLE_APP_ID=
# LENS_DEVICE_TEST_ATTESTATION=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE MARKETPLACE BILL (B20.2) — a paid listing can be used by no one but its seller until this is set
# (except by a test workspace: while no workspace has a bill in Stripe, a test workspace's is kept by Lens
# and paid by the synthetic bill-pay, B17.15 — so testers can buy and pay other companies' agents)
# A buyer's paid marketplace uses are metered onto their own monthly Stripe subscription (needs
# LENS_BILLING_ENABLED and the Stripe keys). In Stripe, make a meter (sum, event name as below,
# customer key stripe_customer_id, value key value) and a monthly metered Price on it of 0.00001¢
# per unit — one unit is one µLXC, so the buyer pays each listing's price at the LXC peg. When the
# invoice is paid (webhook invoice.paid) its uses clear and the sellers earn.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_MARKET_BILL_PRICE_ID=
# LENS_MARKET_METER_EVENT=talyvor_marketplace_use
# B32.39 — each billed use's tax is its own line on the same bill: make a second meter (sum, event name as below,
# the same keys) and a monthly metered Price on it of 0.00001¢ per unit, like the one above, and put its id here
# (and the test-mode twin's in LENS_STRIPE_TEST_MARKET_TAX_PRICE_ID). Unset, a use that owes tax waits, unbilled,
# for an operator; no use owes any until tax registrations are loaded (`lens tax registrations add`).
# LENS_MARKET_TAX_PRICE_ID=
# LENS_MARKET_TAX_METER_EVENT=talyvor_marketplace_tax
# LENS_STRIPE_TEST_MARKET_TAX_PRICE_ID=
# B32.45 — who works out the tax on Talyvor's own sales: test (the tax rows loaded with `lens tax rates import`) or
# stripe (Stripe Tax in test mode, from the registrations in the Stripe account of LENS_STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY, else
# of a test-mode LENS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY). A seller's supply and a VAT number check stay with the tax rows.
# LENS_TAX_PARTNER=test
# B32.40 — Talyvor is the supplier on every marketplace receipt: its name, address and VAT number as the receipts print
# them. Until the VAT number is set every receipt reads "VAT registration pending" and is marked Preview.
# LENS_SUPPLIER_LEGAL_NAME=TALYVOR LTD
# LENS_SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=71-75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London, United Kingdom, WC2H 9JQ
# LENS_SUPPLIER_VAT_NUMBER=
# LENS_MARKET_TRIAL_MAX=5          # the most free trial uses one per_use offer may give each buyer (B32.21)
# LENS_LINEAGE_MAX_SHARE_BPS=3000  # the largest share of a remix's sales a royalty listing may ask, in bps (B32.24)
# LENS_LINEAGE_MAX_DEPTH=5         # how many generations a listing's lineage read walks up, and its royalties are paid (B32.24, B32.26)
# LENS_LINEAGE_TOTAL_CAP_BPS=5000  # the most a listing's parents together receive of what it received from a sale, in bps (B32.26)
# LENS_MARKET_SIMILARITY_HOLD=0.92 # how similar a new version may be to another seller's listing it does not declare as a parent before it is held for review (B32.46)
# LENS_IP_COUNTER_DAYS=10          # how many days a seller has to counter an IP claim against their listing (B32.47)
# LENS_SELLER_TAX_REMINDER_DAYS=30 # the days between the requests to a seller with earnings for their tax details; the third request holds their payouts until they are complete (B32.41)
# LENS_MARKET_PAYOUT_WEEKDAY=MON   # the day of the week, UTC, sellers are paid on: MON to SUN (B32.42)
# LENS_SELF_BILLING_VAT=false      # true once Talyvor's accountant confirms the treatment: a self-billing seller's VAT is worked out and paid with their payout; false issues every self-billed invoice at zero VAT, "under review" (B32.43)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TALYVOR'S FEES (B32.8) — Nicolai's decisions of 5 Oct 2026, each defaulting to his value. internal/fees
# reads them and nothing else holds a fee; GET /v1/public/fees shows them to /pricing. Basis points:
# 100 = 1%. Never set one under docker-compose environment: — an empty value there discards this one.
# MARKET_TAKE: Talyvor's share of a listing sale, rental, subscription or per-use charge (Rooms
# included), from the first dollar of the price before tax; the seller keeps the rest.
# SERVICES_TAKE: of a job, and of a payment to another company's agent. COMPUTE_TAKE: of compute.
# LENDING_FEE: of a loan arranged. PLATFORM_FEE: on AI spend charged to credits, by plan (B32.11: plus,
# pro, max and byok take team's, no plan takes free's, an Enterprise contract may set its own; a call on
# the workspace's own provider keys, or drawn from a chat plan's allowance, carries none). FX_MARGIN:
# over the reference rate on a conversion, by plan. INTL_PAYMENT_FEE_MINOR: per international payment,
# in minor units of its currency, plus the partner's cost. MERCHANT_FEE: accepting a card payment,
# plus card processing; MERCHANT_A2A_FEE: accepting a payment from an account.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_MARKET_TAKE_BPS=1500
# LENS_SERVICES_TAKE_BPS=500
# LENS_COMPUTE_TAKE_BPS=500
# LENS_LENDING_FEE_BPS=100
# LENS_PLATFORM_FEE_BPS={"free":550,"team":300,"business":100,"enterprise":100}
# LENS_FX_MARGIN_BPS={"free":0,"team":50,"business":25,"enterprise":15}
# LENS_INTL_PAYMENT_FEE_MINOR={"GBP":500,"EUR":600,"USD":700}
# LENS_MERCHANT_FEE_BPS=75
# LENS_MERCHANT_A2A_FEE_BPS=100

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT ENTERPRISE COSTS FROM (B32.77) — Nicolai's decision of 5 Oct 2026, "Enterprise from $2,500 a month".
# Whole US cents. Enterprise is contracted, never a Stripe Price, so GET /v1/billing/plans gives /pricing this
# figure as enterprise_from_usd_cents, beside Team's, Business's and BYOK's prices read from Stripe. Never set
# it under docker-compose environment: — an empty value there discards this one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_ENTERPRISE_FROM_USD_CENTS=250000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT EACH PLAN UNLOCKS (B32.12) — Nicolai's decision of 5 Oct 2026; the commented value is the default.
# internal/plans reads it; GET /v1/public/plan-gates shows it to /pricing. Set, it names all four plans.
# agents and seats: how many a workspace may have, -1 unlimited (an archived agent does not count; an
# Enterprise contract may set its own). own_provider_keys: none, add_on (only with the BYOK add-on) or
# included. live_money false keeps every money capability B30 registers, and every RED or AMBER one, on
# test money even with a clearance; true takes each live as it is cleared. plus, pro and max take free's
# gates; byok takes team's, with own keys. A refusal names this setting, the plan and the plan that would
# allow it. Never set it under docker-compose environment: — an empty value there discards this one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_PLAN_GATES={"free":{"agents":3,"seats":1,"own_provider_keys":"none","live_money":false,"slack_teams_approvals":false,"sso":false,"audit_export":false,"edge":false},"team":{"agents":25,"seats":5,"own_provider_keys":"add_on","live_money":true,"slack_teams_approvals":true,"sso":false,"audit_export":false,"edge":false},"business":{"agents":-1,"seats":25,"own_provider_keys":"included","live_money":true,"slack_teams_approvals":true,"sso":true,"audit_export":true,"edge":false},"enterprise":{"agents":-1,"seats":-1,"own_provider_keys":"included","live_money":true,"slack_teams_approvals":true,"sso":true,"audit_export":true,"edge":true}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROOMS PER PLAN — rooms_plan_limits (B32.29); the commented value is the default, and every value is a
# proposal for Nicolai. internal/rooms reads it. Set, it names all four plans; -1 is unlimited.
# public_rooms and private_rooms: the rooms a workspace may have open (a closed room does not count);
# members_per_room (the owner included) and agents_per_room: by the room owner's plan, whoever joins;
# room_budget_max_usd: the largest monthly limit on a room's wallet (B32.32). plus, pro and max take
# team's limits; byok takes business's; any other plan takes free's. A refusal is 402 naming
# rooms_plan_limits and the plan. Never set it under docker-compose environment: — an empty value there
# discards this one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_ROOMS_PLAN_LIMITS={"free":{"public_rooms":3,"private_rooms":0,"members_per_room":50,"agents_per_room":10,"room_budget_max_usd":100},"team":{"public_rooms":25,"private_rooms":10,"members_per_room":250,"agents_per_room":50,"room_budget_max_usd":5000},"business":{"public_rooms":-1,"private_rooms":100,"members_per_room":1000,"agents_per_room":250,"room_budget_max_usd":50000},"enterprise":{"public_rooms":-1,"private_rooms":-1,"members_per_room":-1,"agents_per_room":-1,"room_budget_max_usd":-1}}
# LENS_ROOM_MESSAGES_PER_MINUTE=20  # how many messages one member posts in one room in a minute (B32.30)
# LENS_ROOM_CONTEXT_MESSAGES=30  # how many of a room's latest messages its AI reads with a member's question (B32.33)
# LENS_ROOM_REPORTS_HIDE=3  # how many workspaces' open reports take a public room off the list until it is reviewed (B32.52)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KNOW YOUR AGENT (B30.5) — every agent's credential, a JWT signed with Ed25519 (docs/kya.md). The key is
# base64 of an Ed25519 32-byte seed (`openssl rand -base64 32`). Unset, Lens makes one each time it starts:
# the credentials it signed stay verifiable until they expire, because the JWKS publishes every key a
# credential not yet expired was signed with — but set a fixed one in production. Never set either under
# docker-compose environment: — an empty value there discards this one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_KYA_SIGNING_KEY=
# LENS_KYA_CREDENTIAL_TTL=24h  # how long a credential is valid; the agent is given a new one after

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDENTITY CHECKS (B30.112) — with a Persona API key and its "KYC" inquiry template set, a person's identity
# check (L2) goes to Persona: the owner completes a government ID and a selfie at the link the check gives.
# With a Companies House REST API key set, a UK company's check (L3) reads the Companies House register. Each
# left empty keeps the Test provider for that check, and synthetic workspaces always stay on it. A pass by
# Persona's Sandbox (a persona_sandbox_ key) counts for test money only. Never set them under docker-compose
# environment: — an empty value there discards these.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LENS_PERSONA_API_KEY=
LENS_PERSONA_TEMPLATE_ID=
LENS_COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SANCTIONS SCREENING (B30.6) — every payee and every payment in or out is screened against the UK Sanctions
# List and OFAC's SDN list, which Lens downloads from their official URLs at start and each day. An exact
# match on a listed name refuses the money and opens a compliance case; a name at least this similar to a
# listed one (0 to 1, Jaro-Winkler) holds it for an operator to release or refuse at /v1/admin/screening.
# Nicolai sets the threshold; until he does it is 0.9. Never set it under docker-compose environment: — an
# empty value there discards this one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_SCREENING_FUZZY_THRESHOLD=0.9
# A list that has not downloaded for this many hours is stale: every payment in or out is then held for an
# operator, the operator is alerted at most once an hour, and the status page shows the Sanctions screening rail
# down with the lists' age. Nicolai sets it; until he does it is 48.
# LENS_SCREENING_MAX_AGE_HOURS=48

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRANSACTION MONITORING (B30.7) — rules judge every payment in or out through a partner as it moves, and
# nightly over the last day's. A hit opens or extends the workspace's compliance case (kind monitoring) for an
# operator to review at /v1/admin/screening and /v1/admin/compliance/alerts; it never moves or stops money.
# Each rule's values are a JSON object; a value left out keeps its starting value. Nicolai sets them; until he
# does, each rule uses the starting value below, written in its file in internal/monitoring and listed with
# what it means in docs/compliance-defaults.md. Never set them under docker-compose environment: — an empty
# value there discards these.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How far back a payee counts as already paid, and an agent's payments make its usual size (days).
# LENS_MONITOR_HISTORY_DAYS=90
# Several payments just under an agent's approval amount.
# LENS_MONITOR_UNDER_APPROVAL={"payments":3,"within_hours":24,"under_percent":10}
# Money in and straight out.
# LENS_MONITOR_IN_AND_OUT={"within_minutes":60,"out_percent":50}
# A first payment to a new payee well above the agent's usual size.
# LENS_MONITOR_NEW_PAYEE_LARGE={"times_usual":3,"from_payments":3}
# A burst of round amounts.
# LENS_MONITOR_ROUND_AMOUNTS={"payments":3,"within_minutes":60,"round_to":100}
# Many new payees in one day.
# LENS_MONITOR_NEW_PAYEES={"payees":5,"within_hours":24}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE COMPLIANCE CASE FILE (B30.8): the operator reviews a case at /v1/admin/compliance/cases, freezes or unfreezes
# the workspace's money capabilities, adds notes, closes it with a reason and exports a report draft. Each of those
# actions, and screening's release and refuse, needs the admin key, the operator's name in X-Talyvor-Operator and a
# step-up code in X-Talyvor-Step-Up: the six digits an authenticator app shows for this secret (base32, at least 16
# bytes — e.g. `head -c 20 /dev/urandom | base32`, then add it to the app); each code opens one action. Unset, those
# actions answer 503. Nicolai sets it.
# Never set it under docker-compose environment: — an empty value there discards this one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_OPERATOR_STEP_UP_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AGENT CARDS (B19.12) — TEST MODE ONLY (class RED): each agent may hold a virtual Stripe Issuing card,
# and every purchase is approved or declined in real time by the agent's spending rules and balance.
# LENS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY must be a TEST key (sk_test_…) — with a live key no card is issued. In Stripe
# (test mode): Issuing → settings → real-time authorisations, endpoint
# https://<lens host>/v1/agent-cards/authorizations; its signing secret goes here. Unset, that endpoint
# is 404 and no purchase is approved. Cards are issued in the platform's currency; each purchase is
# priced in USD at the day's ECB reference rate. See docs/agent-cards.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_STRIPE_ISSUING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LENS_STRIPE_ISSUING_CURRENCY=gbp

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SELLER PAYOUTS (B20.5) — sellers connect a Stripe Express account and are paid monthly once they reach
# US$25 (needs LENS_BILLING_ENABLED and the Stripe keys, with Connect turned on in the Stripe dashboard).
# Payouts are USD transfers from the platform's USD balance. Add charge.dispute.created to the webhook
# endpoint's events (a chargeback reverses the seller's earning). Stripe's onboarding returns the seller
# to these pages.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_MARKET_PAYOUT_RETURN_URL=https://app.talyvor.com/marketplace/selling?payouts=connected
# LENS_MARKET_PAYOUT_REFRESH_URL=https://app.talyvor.com/marketplace/selling?payouts=expired

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EVERY OTHER SETTING (B18.11). Each line: the variable, its default, and what it does. Nothing here
# needs setting; uncomment a line only to change it. A setting docker-compose.yaml names under
# `environment:` is not here — set that one in .env (see .env.example). internal/config/
# lens_env_example_test.go fails the build if config.go reads a variable neither file documents.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LENS_ANNOTATION_MINTING_ENABLED=false           # mint for data-labelling annotations; spendable at once, so opt-in
# LENS_ANTIGAMING_AUTO_REVOKE_ENABLED=false       # sweep that finds self-dealing royalty rings and revokes their held mints before settlement
# LENS_ANTIGAMING_INTERVAL=1m                     # how often that anti-gaming sweep runs
# LENS_ANTIGAMING_SCAN_WINDOW=168h                # how far back it scans; must exceed the 72h holdback
# LENS_AUDIT_EXPORT_INTERVAL=1h                   # how often audit events are exported off-box
# LENS_AUDIT_EXPORT_URL=                          # webhook URL that audit events are exported to; empty = no export
# LENS_AUDIT_REQUIRE_EXPORT_BEFORE_PRUNE=false    # retention deletes a token_events row only after it was exported
# LENS_AUDIT_RETENTION=                           # how long token_events are kept (Go duration, e.g. 8760h); empty/0 = forever
# LENS_AUDIT_RETENTION_DATABASE_URL=              # the lens_retention role's direct Postgres URL the sweeper deletes with; empty = Lens's own login (docs/AUDIT-POLICY.md)
# LENS_BURST_MULTIPLIER=1.5                       # how far above the rate limit a short burst may go
# LENS_CB_RESET_TIMEOUT=                          # circuit breaker: how long a tripped provider stays open; empty = library default
# LENS_CB_THRESHOLD=                              # circuit breaker: consecutive failures that trip it; empty = library default
# LENS_CONFIDENTIAL_MINTING_ENABLED=false         # mint paying a node for verified confidential-compute capacity
# LENS_CONFIDENTIAL_RATE_PER_POINT=0              # LENS per epoch for that mint; 0 = inert
# LENS_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=                      # comma-separated origins allowed to call the API from a browser; empty = same-origin only
# LENS_DASHBOARD_ENABLED=false                    # serve the built-in browser page at /dashboard
# LENS_DB_MIN_CONNS=2                             # idle Postgres connections kept open
# LENS_DB_REPLICA_URL=                            # optional read-replica DSN for analytics and display reads; money reads stay on the primary
# LENS_DB_SSL_MODE=require                        # Postgres TLS (libpq sslmode: disable, require, verify-ca, verify-full)
# LENS_DETECTOR_SWEEP_ENABLED=true                # scheduled cache and distill abuse detectors (needs the economy on)
# LENS_DETECTOR_SWEEP_INTERVAL=1h                 # how often the detectors run
# LENS_DETECTOR_SWEEP_WINDOW=24h                  # how far back each detector run looks
# LENS_DETECT_BILATERAL_MIN_FRAC=0.9              # detector: share of mints between one pair that flags a two-party ring (0..1)
# LENS_DETECT_BILATERAL_MIN_MINTS=20              # detector: mints a pair needs before the bilateral check applies
# LENS_DETECT_SIMILARITY_MAX_STDDEV=0.02          # detector: similarity spread below which requests look scripted
# LENS_DETECT_SIMILARITY_MIN_SAMPLE=30            # detector: requests needed before the similarity check applies
# LENS_DETECT_VOLUME_MAX_REQUESTERS=2             # detector: at most this many requesters behind a high-volume earner flags it
# LENS_DETECT_VOLUME_MIN_MINTS=50                 # detector: mints needed before the volume check applies
# LENS_DISTILL_MINT_CAP_WINDOW=24h                # rolling window of the distill mint cap
# LENS_DISTILL_WORKER_BIN=                        # path to the distill-worker binary; default: next to the lens binary
# LENS_EARN_REQUIRE_LIVE_PURCHASE=false           # only a real-money purchase verifies a workspace to earn (test purchases no longer count)
# LENS_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=                        # embedding endpoint override; empty = OpenAI
# LENS_EVAL_CONTRIBUTION_MINTING_ENABLED=false    # mint paying for eval contributions that discriminate between models
# LENS_EVAL_CONTRIBUTION_RATE_PER_POINT=0.05      # LENS per discrimination point for that mint
# LENS_GLOBAL_RPM=0                               # requests per minute across all workspaces; 0 = no cap
# LENS_GLOBAL_TPM=0                               # tokens per minute across all workspaces; 0 = no cap
# LENS_GUARDRAILS_ENABLED=false                   # output guardrails (PII, JSON/length/regex checks) and their per-workspace config API
# LENS_GUARDRAILS_RELOAD_INTERVAL=30s             # how often each replica reloads custom guardrail policies
# LENS_H5_ARTIFACT_ENABLED=false                  # POST /v1/outputs/{id}/artifact: commit a buildable artifact to an output
# LENS_H5_ATTEST_ENABLED=false                    # Talyvor reproduces a bonded output's build and records the verdict (admin-only)
# LENS_H5_BONDS_ENABLED=false                     # provenance bonds: collateral on an output, burned in part on a reported failure (money path)
# LENS_HA_ENABLED=false                           # run as one of several replicas with leader election (needs LENS_REDIS_URL)
# LENS_JWT_SECRET=                                # REMOVED: the old HS256 secret; if set, Lens refuses to start (use an EC P-256 key)
# LENS_K4_VERIFIER_ENABLED=false                  # after serving, check the output against the constraints the request declared (JSON schema, tool args)
# LENS_KEEL_DEVIATION_SIGMA=2                     # drift sweep: deviation, in sigmas, that counts as drift
# LENS_KEEL_ENABLED=true                          # cross-tenant drift-attribution sweep (read-only, never touches money)
# LENS_KEEL_HARDENED_ENABLED=true                 # money-grade drift detection on top of the sweep
# LENS_KEEL_HARDENED_SIGMA=3.5                    # hardened drift: robust (MAD-scaled) score that counts as drift
# LENS_KEEL_MIN_SAMPLES=30                        # drift: requests a workspace needs in a window to be scored
# LENS_KEEL_MONEY_COHORT_FLOOR=10                 # hardened drift: smallest cohort whose findings may affect money
# LENS_KEEL_PERSISTENCE_WINDOWS=3                 # hardened drift: consecutive windows a finding must last
# LENS_KEEL_ROYALTY_HAIRCUT_ENABLED=true          # lower (never raise) reuse royalties for a workspace with sustained drift
# LENS_KEEL_WINDOW_SECONDS=3600                   # drift sweep window, in seconds
# LENS_LATENCY_MINTING_ENABLED=false              # mint paying a node for fast, quality-gated service
# LENS_LATENCY_RATE_PER_POINT=0                   # LENS per latency point for that mint; 0 = inert
# LENS_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080                   # address the HTTP server listens on (ignored when LENS_TLS_DOMAIN is set)
# LENS_LOCAL_ENDPOINTS=                           # local model endpoints, provider:url:model1,model2;provider:url:model3
# LENS_LXC_GATING_ENABLED=false                   # refuse a request (402) when the workspace's LXC balance cannot cover it
# LENS_LXC_SHADOW_SPEND_ENABLED=false             # record a shadow LXC debit after each served call, alongside the real charge
# LENS_MAX_CACHE_TTL=24h                          # longest a cached answer may live
# LENS_NATS_TLS=false                             # use TLS to NATS (or put tls:// in LENS_NATS_URL)
# LENS_NATS_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=false                 # skip NATS certificate verification (self-signed certificates only)
# LENS_NODE_ATTESTATION_VERIFY_ENABLED=false      # verify nodes' confidential-compute attestations (NVIDIA NRAS)
# LENS_NODE_AUTOROUTE_ENABLED=false               # route normal inference traffic to registered inference nodes
# LENS_NODE_LATENCY_CAPTURE_ENABLED=false         # record each node's serve latency per cohort (descriptive)
# LENS_NODE_PRIVATE_CIDR_ALLOWLIST=               # comma-separated private CIDRs nodes may be reached on (e.g. 10.42.0.0/16)
# LENS_NODE_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=false                 # skip certificate verification when calling nodes (self-signed only)
# LENS_OBS_WRITE_MAX_CONCURRENT=32                # post-serve observational writes at once; beyond this they are dropped
# LENS_PATTERN_CONCENTRATION_VELOCITY_MAX=2000    # held pattern mints per workspace per hour above which its mints are withheld
# LENS_PATTERN_EARN_CAP_PER_WORKSPACE=50000       # most routing-pattern credits one workspace earns per window
# LENS_PATTERN_EARN_CAP_WINDOW=24h                # window of the pattern earn cap
# LENS_POOL_CONSUMER_DISCOUNT=0.3                 # share of a pooled cache hit's list price given back to the consumer, [0,1)
# LENS_POOL_HOLDBACK_WINDOW=72h                   # how long a pool royalty stays held before it settles
# LENS_POVI_CHALLENGE_RATE=0.1                    # share of verified node receipts challenged each round, [0,1]
# LENS_POVI_MINTING_ENABLED=false                 # provisional LENS minting from node receipts
# LENS_POVI_MIN_STAKE=100                         # LENS a node must stake to be eligible to mint
# LENS_POVI_SLASH_FRACTION=0.5                    # share of a node's stake burned on a failed challenge, (0,1]
# LENS_POVI_UNBOND_PERIOD=168h                    # how long unbonding stake stays locked and slashable
# LENS_PROOF_OF_BENCHMARK_ENABLED=false           # scheduler that probes nodes with private eval items
# LENS_PROOF_OF_IMPROVEMENT_ENABLED=false         # allow a non-cost reward anchor for improvement mints
# LENS_REDIS_TLS=false                            # use TLS to Redis (or use rediss:// in LENS_REDIS_URL)
# LENS_REDIS_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=false                # skip Redis certificate verification (self-signed certificates only)
# LENS_REPUTATION_BONDED_MINTING_ENABLED=false    # scale receipt and royalty mints by the contributor's reputation (never up)
# LENS_RETRY_INITIAL_DELAY=                       # first retry delay to a provider; empty = library default
# LENS_RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=                        # provider retry attempts; empty/0 = library default
# LENS_RETRY_MAX_DELAY=                           # longest retry delay; empty = library default
# LENS_ROI_INCLUDE_ENGINEER_BREAKDOWN=false       # show cost per named engineer in the ROI report (sensitive)
# LENS_ROUTING_BRAIN_ENABLED=false                # offline learner that writes a best-model recommendation per workspace and cohort
# LENS_ROUTING_DECISION_CAPTURE_ENABLED=true      # record each routing decision: baseline vs served model and cost
# LENS_ROUTING_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=false         # let mined routing patterns influence model selection
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_ENABLED=false           # accept routing predictions ("cohort C -> model M") from contributors
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_MINTING_ENABLED=false   # mint paying for a prediction proven better than baseline
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_RATE_PER_POINT=0.02     # LENS per skill-margin point for that mint
# LENS_ROUTING_PREDICTION_SCORING_ENABLED=false   # sweeper that scores routing predictions against a held eval slice
# LENS_ROUTING_TIER_COHORTS_ENABLED=false         # routing intelligence picks the best model per complexity tier
# LENS_SEMANTIC_CACHE_SWEEP_INTERVAL=1h           # how often the semantic-cache retention sweeper runs
# LENS_TARE_MODEL_DIR=/models/kompress-small     # Tare phase 2a: where the kompress-small weights are (the image carries them here)
# LENS_TLS_CACHE_DIR=/var/cache/lens-tls          # where Let's Encrypt certificates are cached
# LENS_TLS_DOMAIN=                                # public hostname to get a Let's Encrypt certificate for; set = serve :443 and :80
# LENS_TOKEN_TTL=24h                              # lifetime of an issued session token
# LENS_TRUSTFUL_COMPUTE_MINT_ENABLED=false        # LEGACY per-request compute mint with no receipt; leave off
# LENS_WORKSPACE_MAX_STALENESS=1m30s              # past this without a workspace reload, privacy settings fail closed
# LENS_WORKSPACE_RELOAD_INTERVAL=30s              # how often each replica reloads workspace settings
# LENS_WORKTIER_ENABLED=false                     # classify each served request by size, cost, complexity and sensitivity
